    "notes": "PMTiles identifies the station footprint, platform bodies and alignments. The long station wall sets the heading. Nine entrance samples, fifteen stair probes and seventeen track lanes clear the station terrain cuts in each tier. The model represents the existing station and its above-ground public circulation. Future redevelopment, temporary roof works, train animation and underground platforms are outside this model. Track centerlines and platform footprints follow PMTiles. Three eastern tracks are reconstructed from mapped platform stops and the parallel track alignment where centerlines are absent. Roof sections, gables and internal elevations are photo-based reconstructions. The upper entrances fit standard terrain samples and the tracks use an estimated lower station datum. Neighboring commercial and hotel buildings remain independent map objects. Their station-side approaches share the fitted station terrain cutout."
  },
